# =============================================================================
# Virtual IIoT Security Testbed — environment configuration TEMPLATE
# Research internship: "Identifying and Prioritizing Vulnerabilities in IIoT
# and Industry 4.0 Systems" (BSUIR)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO USE:
#   cp .env.example .env      # create your local, private copy
#   # edit .env with real values (see notes below)
#   docker compose up -d      # Compose reads .env automatically
#
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed. This template is safe to
# publish because it contains only placeholders.
#
# RESEARCH NOTE: these credentials are themselves part of the attack surface
# under study (the "weak / exposed authentication" scenario, internship Task 3).
# For controlled experiments you may WANT deliberately weak values here — but
# keep the stack on an isolated network and never reuse real passwords.
# =============================================================================

# --- InfluxDB (historian: stores captured Modbus/MQTT telemetry) ----------
# Used by the influxdb service and by Node-RED / Grafana to read & write the
# time-series data your feature extraction (Task 4) will draw on.
INFLUXDB_USERNAME=admin
INFLUXDB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_strong_password
INFLUXDB_ORG=iiot
INFLUXDB_BUCKET=telemetry
# API token Node-RED and Grafana use to talk to InfluxDB.
# Generate a real one:  openssl rand -hex 32
INFLUXDB_ADMIN_TOKEN=CHANGE_ME_run_openssl_rand_hex_32

# --- Grafana (dashboards over the historian) ------------------------------
GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=admin
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_strong_password

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not templated here (documented in README instead), because they are either
# app-internal defaults or deliberately insecure test conditions:
#   - OpenPLC web login ...... openplc / openplc  (default; a weak-auth target)
#   - FUXA editor ............ token auth disabled (an open-HMI test condition)
#   - Mosquitto MQTT ......... allow_anonymous true (insecure-comms test target)
# These are intentional parts of the vulnerability study, not oversights.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
